from ./Determinism import Determinism
from ./structure import StructuralContext
from ./meaning/Provenance import Provenance

export anchor Principles:
    description:
        A few principles decide every question this section answers. When a
        rule seems arbitrary, one of these is usually the reason for it.

    whereTruthComesFrom:
        ```text
        the specification defines the truth
        analysis extracts and normalizes it
        the implementation agent implements it
        ```

        Analysis never adds to the truth. If an implementation is wrong
        because a requirement was wrong, the requirement leads back to the
        words that stated it, and those words are what get fixed.

    whatAnalysisDoes:
        ```text
        extract what can be known
        normalize what can be normalized
        resolve what can be resolved
        keep everything else as unresolved
        ```

        Unknown information is a valid result. So is ambiguity, and so is a
        statement analysis could not read. An interpretation analysis made
        up is never a valid result, however plausible it is.

    structureFirst:
        Piton structure is checked by the compiler, and prose is not. So
        structure is read first, and it decides how prose is read, as
        described in @{StructuralContext}. An explicit reference always
        outranks a name that merely looks like it matches.

    trustOverCleverness:
        Analysis is not trying to understand as much as possible. It is
        trying to be right about everything it claims to understand. False
        certainty is worse than an honest unknown, for the reasons given in
        @{Determinism}.

    everythingIsTraceable:
        Every fact, open item and instruction can be followed back to the
        text or structure it came from, and every statement can be followed
        forward to everything that came from it, as described in
        @{Provenance}.

    readingThisSection:
        Properties named example or examples, and every code block, only
        illustrate. They never add a rule. Every other property states rules.
        When an example and a rule disagree, the rule is right and the example
        is a mistake in this specification.
